    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nPilot View is a highly regarded, private residential development renowned for its strong sense of community, beautifully maintained waterfront gardens, and exceptional convenience, just a short stroll from Dalkey Town and the DART. Occupying a prime ground-floor position within this secure gated enclave, no 2 Inishowen enjoys breathtaking, uninterrupted views across Dublin Bay to Howth. A private seafront terrace provides the perfect vantage point to soak in the ever-changing coastal panorama, with the sea quite literally on your doorstep.\n\nExtending to approximately 83 sq.m (893sq.ft), the accommodation is both bright and well proportioned. A welcoming entrance hall with practical coat storage leads to a spacious living room featuring an open fireplace and direct access to the sea-facing terrace. The kitchen/breakfast room is equally impressive, framed by a large picture window that captures spectacular coastal views, creating an idyllic setting for morning coffee or relaxed dining while watching boats go by and seabirds along the shoreline.\nThere are two generous double bedrooms, both benefitting from fitted wardrobes, while the principal bedroom enjoys the added luxury of an en-suite bathroom and access to front communal gardens. A family bathroom completes the accommodation.\n\nThe property further benefits from surface parking, three communal electric vehicle charging points, and a particularly useful private storage locker.\n\nPerfectly positioned between Dalkey and Sandycove, Pilot View offers immediate access to an excellent selection of boutique shops, cafés, restaurants, gastropubs and everyday amenities. Outdoor enthusiasts are spoiled for choice with scenic coastal walks along Coliemore Road, Harbour Road and Vico Road, while the ever-popular Killiney Hill is close by. Excellent transport links include nearby DART stations at Dalkey, Sandycove & Glasthule, and Glenageary, together with easy access to the N11, M50 and several bus routes. Further shopping and leisure amenities can be found in Sandycove, Glasthule and Dun Laoghaire.\n\nCombining an unrivalled coastal setting, outstanding convenience and enormous potential to create a truly special home, 2 Inishowen, Pilot View presents a rare opportunity that must be viewed to be fully appreciated."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \ngenerous hallway with coat storage.\n\nLiving Room - \nA spacious and light filled room with a tall ceiling height, direct coastal views across Dublin Bay to Howth, feature open fireplace, tv/internet point and patio door onto an outdoor terrace with direct garden access.\n\nKitchen - \nwith a selection of fitted wall and floor units, granite counter tops, tiled splashback, stainless steel sink unit, extractor fan, hob and oven.\n\nDining/Breakfast - \nopen plan off the kitchen, with a large picture window with direct sea views.\n\nBedroom 1 - \ndouble bedroom to the front of the property with fitted wardrobes and a door opening out to the front communal gardens.\n\nEn-Suite - \nfully tiled with w.c, bath and sink unit. A window provides natural ventilation to the room.\n\nBedroom 2 - \ndouble bedroom to the front with fitted wardrobes.\n\nShower Room - \nfully tiled with w.c, vanity sink unit, mirror and shower cubicle.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Spacious apartment overlooking the sea</li><li> Direct access onto the landscaped communal gardens</li><li> Large outdoor terrace overlooking the sea </li><li> Two spacious double bedrooms (1 ensuite)</li><li> Gas fired central heating</li><li> Secure storage unit</li><li> Car parking set behind electronic gates</li><li> Annual service charge approx. 750 per quarter</ul>"
      },
